---
import AplusPage from '../../layouts/AplusPage.astro';
---
<AplusPage title="UI Wiki | A+ Active Services" eyebrow="Wiki / UI" heading="Healthcare UI should guide action, not decorate uncertainty." intro="The interface should make the recommendation, evidence, safety note, and next action visible at the right moment.">
  <section class="aplus-screen-stack" aria-label="Healthcare UI decision model">
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">Metacognition steering</p>
      <h2>Every screen should make judgment easier before it makes automation faster.</h2>
      <p>The buyer should see the recommendation, evidence, safety note, and next action in one glance, especially when the workflow touches clinical, operational, or revenue context.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">Mobile conversion</p>
      <h2>The first viewport has to support a real decision.</h2>
      <p>Most traffic will come from phones, so the screen should preserve proof of humanity, one CTA, and a clear path to newsletter, community, event calendar, or booking.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-flywheel-strip" aria-label="Healthcare UI parts">
    <span>Recommendation</span>
    <span>Evidence</span>
    <span>Safety</span>
    <span>Next action</span>
    <span>Feedback</span>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-content-grid">
    <article><h2>One recommendation</h2><p>Make the primary next step obvious before showing secondary options.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Evidence nearby</h2><p>Put the reason, source, and caveat close to the action it supports.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Mobile first</h2><p>Most visitors arrive on a phone, so the core CTA and proof must survive the small viewport.</p></article>
  </section>
</AplusPage>
